commit 8694fb1a5759d057ef66b3a1de07d52309a68d02
Author: admin <admin@MacBook-Pro-de-admin.local>
Date:   Tue Aug 25 08:31:04 2026 -0400

    feat: parameterize the bonding curve — brand's fast/medium/slow now real
    
    Every market read the same five hardcoded SigmoidMath constants
    (b=500, c=100_000, P=1000, a=100/200) regardless of its own supply cap
    or the fast/medium/slow shape a brand picked in the campaign wizard —
    that choice was captured for display only (CampaignRecord.curveShape)
    and never reached the contract. Concretely broken for every demo
    product: with a fixed b=500 inflection and real supply caps of
    20-60, the curve never gets anywhere near its own inflection point,
    so price barely moves at all across a product's whole real supply
    range (~$915-920 the entire way, confirmed numerically) regardless of
    what price range was configured.
    
    - contracts/src/SigmoidMath.sol: getPrice/getTotalCost now take a
      CurveParams struct (b/c/p/aPrimary/aSecondary) instead of hardcoded
      constants. Same formula, now per-market.
    - contracts/src/IMPXMarket.sol: five new immutables replace
      INFLECTION_POINT; constructor takes a CurveParams struct (structs
      can't be immutable directly, so it's unpacked into the five fields).
      Every SigmoidMath call site updated.
    - agents/src/valet/curve.ts (new): deriveCurveParams(minPrice, maxPrice,
      totalSupply, curveShape) — the actual derivation. b scales to the
      market's own supply cap instead of a fixed 500; c = k·b² per shape
      (fast=0.15/medium=0.4/slow=1.0, medium's ratio is exactly the
      original constants'); P and the two amplitudes solved so
      price(0)=minPrice, price(totalSupply)=maxPrice, and the original
      "secondary zone is 2x steeper" asymmetry holds. Verified numerically:
      reproduces the original curve almost exactly at its own reference
      scale (medium/1000/~$916-1168), correctly makes a flat curve when
      min===max (the wizard's "Flat Price" mode), stays monotonic across
      200 randomized configs, and actually spans a demo-scale (50-unit)
      product's configured price range instead of the ~$5 total movement
      the old fixed curve gave it.
    - Wired into the only three places that ever deploy an IMPXMarket:
      valet/index.ts's live createCampaign() (uses the brand's real
      basePriceUsdc/maxPriceUsdc/curveShape — already being collected,
      just never used), deployDemoProducts.ts (fixed $850-$1200/medium
      reference range, scaled per product's own supply cap — a pure scale
      fix, not a pricing change), migrateCampaignContracts.ts (same,
      reading each campaign's actual configured range).
    - contracts/test/POPZ.t.sol: 63/63 passing (62 previous + 1 new —
      test_Sigmoid_Parameterized_DifferentMarketsDifferentCurves,
      demonstrating the exact bug/fix numerically in-contract).
    
    Not yet done: the 54 live markets still run the old fixed curve until
    redeployed — this is a contract-level change only, same shape as the
    registry migration (new addresses, needs re-authorization + liquidity
    reseed). Flagging before running it rather than doing it unprompted.

